		<SWE></SWE>
		<SWF></SWF>
		<Meldungstext>\T\L\S\K\AStatus of radio clock receiver:\L\S\K\N
 On input of a value \L\B\K\N&gt; 0\L\S\K\N in \L\B\K\N adaption channel 19 \L\S\K\N(radio clock synchronization time) the test mode for the radio clock receiver is started. In this mode, the receiver's signals are checked for 10 seconds. During this measurement \L\B\K\NMeasurement \L\S\K\Nis also displayed in \L\B\K\NMVB 2\L\S\K\N. If the measurement is successful, meaning the wiring to the receiver is OK, \L\R\K\NReceiver OK \L\S\K\Nis also displayed \L\B\K\NMVB 2\L\S\K\N. This safeguards the radio clock function. If \L\R\K\NReceiver n.OK\L\S\K\N is displayed, however, either the receiver is not correctly connected or the reception range is inadequate. When the test mode is quit, \L\R\K\NTest off\L\S\K\N is displayed. By briefly setting the channel to \L\B\K\N0 \L\S\K\Nand entering a number \L\B\K\N &gt; 0\L\S\K\N the test mode can be restarted.
</Meldungstext>
		<Requests>
		</Requests>
